From 1aae6c6f6d1f0e5153453ab65d940a4431ef6f9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 18:38:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Single-source thermodynamics and NumPy grid validation

Move the ideal-gas and Euler-Lagrange formulas into equicdft.thermodynamics
(density_weighted_integral, log_dimensionless_density, ideal_free_energy,
local_chemical_potential, beta_external_potential) and route the model,
the GridData pipeline, the density-noise augmentation, the solver residual
and line search, the fixed-dipole ideal functional and the LJ regression
harness through them. energy.py keeps only the readout interface.

stencil.canonical_grid_order (GridOrder) is now the one NumPy validator of
a complete zero-based regular grid; grid_size_array / grid_spacing_array
replace the private _data_helpers metadata coercions. process_atoms,
coarsen_grid and get_neighbor_indices share it.

LJ forward/solve gates are bit-identical to the metalwall-polar snapshot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CKJKJnMQ5g5crBBPsN5iZn
