From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 18:45:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Make the loss-term and metric protocols explicit

LossTerm(nn.Module) is the base of every named, weighted scalar loss:
evaluate(outputs, batch, model=None) returns {"loss", ...details} and
forward returns the scalar. TensorLoss, FourierResponseLoss and
FourierStabilityLoss subclass it; Loss accepts only LossTerm objects,
passes the model to every term and records details for every term.

MetricCollection(nn.Module) is the base of Metrics and
FourierResponseMetrics with update_metrics(subset, outputs, batch,
details=None), retrieve_metrics and clear_metrics; FourierResponseMetrics
reads details[loss_name]. Trainer and TrainingStream check isinstance
instead of probing requires_model / provides_details /
requires_loss_details attributes. Both bases are exported.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CKJKJnMQ5g5crBBPsN5iZn
