From 8eae2853d0d0ee39ef4bc0c319309886905aa526 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:16:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Give readouts one typed ReadoutContext and let the model
 own mean_density

energy.ReadoutContext replaces the ad-hoc context dictionary: the model
fills the primitives of one batch (rho, normalized temperature, voxel
volume, density scale, grid geometry, beta / reference energy /
free-energy mode, invariant features, center density, polarization) and
readouts compose their inputs through cached normalized_rho(),
temperature_feature(), local_features(), pointwise_state() and
state_features(); require(name) raises a KeyError naming a primitive the
model did not supply. ReadoutContext.from_data builds it from a GridData
batch under an explicit unit contract, for the model and for standalone
readout evaluation. Local, Bulk, LongRange, LDA, GGA, Pairwise and
MetalWall readouts consume the context; requires_state_features is gone.

EnergyReadout declares requires_local_features, requires_local_density_index,
requires_dipole_density and n_types; GridCACEModel checks a declared
feature-module contract instead of getattr/hasattr probing, flattens the
invariant block without n_feature_axes, and calls the public
CartesianAFeatures.polarization_fields.

GridCACEModel now owns the single density scale: mean_density defaults to
a_features.mean_density, must agree with it when both are given, and is
required only by readouts that normalize densities. LDAReadout loses its
mean_density argument and buffer. Model files are format version 2;
version-1 payloads are migrated in memory (serialization.migrate_model_payload),
the legacy pickle upgrade moves the scale onto the model, and the LJ
regression fixture is re-saved as version 2 (sha in provenance.json).

LJ forward/solve gates are bit-identical.

