From 4a00ea436616f36b02041273cb254092e60657f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:24:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Complete readout construction at model construction time

LocalReadout and GGAReadout no longer use LazyLinear: they are unbound until
bind_input_size(n_features) builds their network (idempotent for the same
width, ValueError for a different one, RuntimeError on forward while
unbound, is_bound property). GridCACEModel computes the local feature width
(center channels + (1 + n_messages) * n_radial * n_B * n_channels + 1),
binds every local-feature readout in __init__ and casts freshly built
layers to the feature module's dtype and device; n_local_features is
exposed. EnergyReadout.bind_input_size is a documented no-op hook.

Consequences: Trainer loses the first-batch materialization and
_has_uninitialized_parameters, load_checkpoint loses model_kwargs,
model_payload rejects unbound readouts instead of lazy parameters, the
legacy upgrade recovers n_features from a pickled first layer, and
build_mlp always receives a width. BChiMessage.bind_geometry /
stencil_basis and CartesianAFeatures.bessel_stencil_basis are the public
geometry-binding interface the model uses.

LJ forward/solve gates are bit-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CKJKJnMQ5g5crBBPsN5iZn
