From 137a0f066dbe61ce454a8276520de6be021f5a35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:30:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] MetalWall follows the default dtype; reject
 double-counted wrapped readouts

MetalWall validated its electrode geometry in float64 and kept it there, so
a wall built under the float32 default mixed dtypes with the rest of the
model: forward failed in lu_solve and save_model refused the model, which
serialization.build_model papered over with a model-wide cast. The
buffers are now stored in the default floating dtype active at
construction (double-precision geometry: construct under a float64
default), _evaluate_field casts the positions to the working dtype, and
the build_model cast is gone.

EnergyReadout.wrapped_readouts() declares readouts whose energy a wrapper
already includes (MetalWall returns its liquid_coulomb); GridCACEModel
rejects a readout list that contains a wrapped readout beside its wrapper,
or the same module twice, instead of silently counting the liquid Coulomb
energy twice. METAL_WALL.md documents both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CKJKJnMQ5g5crBBPsN5iZn
