From 8076e4f55cf7286f04db72b514ce3e0045c6b370 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 20:14:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Migrate old training checkpoints and harden the
 density-scale migration

Follow-ups from review: Trainer.load_checkpoint now moves version-1
readout.<i>.mean_density entries onto the model through
serialization.migrate_model_state_dict, so checkpoints written before
model format 2 resume; the file, state and legacy-pickle migrations reject
readouts whose scales disagree (within allclose) instead of keeping the
first one silently, and prefer the feature module's scale as the old
constructor did. The message-layer contract on a_features (stencil_basis,
local_density_positions, polarization_fields, bessel_stencil_basis,
max_power, powers, coordinate_scaling) is checked at construction, the
dead CartesianBFeatures.n_feature_axes is gone and the B layout is stated
in the contract, thermodynamics.equilibrium_log_density replaces the
solver's inline Picard target, and polarization.md no longer describes
first-forward width inference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CKJKJnMQ5g5crBBPsN5iZn
